  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "gf_sdp_info_parse",
    "file": "gpac/src/ietf/sdp.c",
    "description": "In the 'r' (repeat times) SDP line parsing, gf_sdp_info_parse writes to timing->OffsetFromStart[timing->NbRepeatOffsets] before checking the upper bound. When NbRepeatOffsets reaches GF_SDP_MAX_TIMEOFFSET (10), the next parsed offset is written at index 10 (out of bounds for u32[10]), then NbRepeatOffsets is incremented and only afterward compared to the max. This causes the UBSan OOB at sdp.c:647.",
    "conditions": "The harness feeds attacker-controlled SDP text into rtpin_load_sdp -> gf_sdp_info_parse. A valid sequence that creates a timing block ('t=') followed by an 'r=' line containing more than GF_SDP_MAX_TIMEOFFSET repeat-offset tokens triggers it. In this PoV, malformed/minimal SDP still reaches the 'r' parser loop and causes NbRepeatOffsets to hit 10, then one extra token causes an out-of-bounds write to OffsetFromStart[10]."
  },
